  "headline": "Gibran Rakabuming Raka Resigns As Vice President Of Indonesia",
  "seoTitle": "Gibran Rakabuming Raka Resigns As Vice President",
  "metaDescription": "Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka has formally submitted his resignation to the MPR, which has 60 days to facilitate the selection of a successor.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka officially submitted his resignation letter to the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) on Thursday.",
    "MPR Chairman Ahmad Muzani confirmed receipt of the document and stated that the institution will immediately begin processing the transition.",
    "According to the constitution, President Prabowo Subianto must propose two candidates to the MPR, which then has 60 days to appoint a new successor."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "On November 12, 2026, Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka formally resigned from his position, submitting his official letter to the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) in Jakarta. Prior to delivering the document to parliamentary leadership, the Vice President held a meeting with President Prabowo Subianto. MPR Chairman Ahmad Muzani confirmed that the assembly would initiate the necessary procedural steps immediately. Under Article 8 of the 1945 Constitution, the government faces a 60-day window to finalize the appointment of a new vice president. During this period, the President is required to present two candidates to the MPR, which will then vote to elect a permanent replacement. The resignation has triggered rapid media coverage and legislative activity as the administration moves to ensure constitutional continuity following the departure.",
  "whyItIsViral": "The story is highly viral due to the sudden nature of the Vice President's resignation and the immediate constitutional process triggered, resulting in maximum coverage velocity across major Indonesian outlets.",
